# Cursor Rules

## Code Quality

- No emoji characters in source code
- No inline imports in Python (all imports at file top)
- No unnecessary one-liner docstrings
- No empty catch blocks
- No broad exception swallowing (except Exception: pass)
- Auto-format on save (ruff/prettier/gofmt/shfmt as available)

## Style

- Write in natural, flowing prose (no staccato)
- No AI-style narrative comments ("Gets the user", "Sets the value")
- Comments only for non-obvious WHY (constraints, invariants, workarounds)
- No double dashes or em dashes in prose

## Behavior

- Investigate before acting. Read code, configs, logs before making changes.
- Fact-check claims. Verify independently.
- No shortcuts. If the honest answer is hard work, say so.
- One recommendation, not a menu.
- Push back when something feels wrong.

## Python

- Always use `uv` for environments (never system pip)
- No `gh` CLI usage

## Safety

- Never deploy to production unless explicitly instructed
- Never force-push to main/master
